<body class="error404 wp-embed-responsive wp-theme-oxygen-is-not-a-theme  oxygen-body" >




										<article id="post-7260" class="post-7260 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-application-management category-general category-numecent-cloudpaging">
					<header>
						<h1>CloudPaging Apps with Citrix</h1>					</header>

					<div>
						
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Anyone who has been around <a href="https://www.citrix.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Citrix</a> for any length of time will know that one of the main challenges is how to manage your template (or gold image) to keep applications up to date.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There are many ways you can achieve this including:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Update a template containing all of your manually installed apps</li>



<li>Use an automated build to freshly install the latest versions of each app</li>



<li>Use AppAttach – this is limited to MSIX and AppV applications only</li>



<li>Use AppV – this is end of life in 2026</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">These methods are all time-consuming or imperfect, but there is another way – Numecent CloudPager.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="831" height="157" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPaging.png" alt="CloudPaging with Citrix" class="wp-image-7251" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPaging.png 831w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPaging-300x57.png 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPaging-768x145.png 768w" sizes="(max-width: 831px) 100vw, 831px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">CloudPager is an application container management system for Windows desktop. It can deliver MSIX and AppV applications, but crucially it can also deliver Numecent’s own CloudPaging apps.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="636" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPager-Applications.png" alt="Numecent CloudPager Applications" class="wp-image-7254" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPager-Applications.png 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPager-Applications-300x186.png 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPager-Applications-768x477.png 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">CloudPaging is a rarity among application virtualisation technologies in that its claim that it can virtualise any application is pretty much true. The traditional limitations of AppV and MSIX do not apply here due to the unique way that CloudPaging can differentiate between components and using “layers” can choose to virtualise them or physically install them – this means that device drivers for example are not a problem.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">What does this mean for your Citrix persona management? It means that you can simply have a template that contains the Windows operating system only and then quickly and dynamically stream in your applications. The Cloud Player agent acts in the background and populates the users Desktop and Start Menu with the shortcuts to applications they need for their role based on “pods” or groups of applications. Compared with other streaming technologies, Cloud Player is very fast, and applications start instantly for the user.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-video"><video autoplay controls loop muted src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPager-Apps-UI-vid.mp4"></video></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Updating application versions is fast and dynamic too. No need for installation or downtime, just update your application or pod with the new version, remove the old version and almost instantly the user is up to date. It’s equally easy to roll back if you need to.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At <a href="https://workspace-it.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Workspace IT</a>, we have an Application Packaging team who are comfortable with all the leading technologies from the traditional Windows Installer MSI to <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/windows/microsoft-desktop-optimization-pack/appv-v4/overview-of-application-virtualization" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">AppV</a>, <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/msix/overview" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">MSIX</a>, <a href="https://workspace-it.com/blog/psappdeploytoolkit-what-is-it-and-why-do-we-use-it/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">PSADT</a> and of course <a href="https://www.numecent.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">CloudPaging</a>.</p>
					</div>

				</article>
								<article id="post-7250" class="post-7250 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-application-management category-general category-numecent-cloudpaging">
					<header>
						<h1>Numecent CloudPaging and CloudPager</h1>					</header>

					<div>
						
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At Workspace IT, we have an Application Packaging team who are comfortable with all the leading technologies from the traditional Windows Installer MSI to <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/windows/microsoft-desktop-optimization-pack/appv-v4/overview-of-application-virtualization" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">AppV</a>, <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/msix/overview" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">MSIX</a> and <a href="https://workspace-it.com/blog/psappdeploytoolkit-what-is-it-and-why-do-we-use-it/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">PSADT</a>. However, one of our favourites is <a href="https://www.numecent.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">CloudPaging</a> from Numecent.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="831" height="157" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPaging.png" alt="Numecent" class="wp-image-7251" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPaging.png 831w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPaging-300x57.png 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/CloudPaging-768x145.png 768w" sizes="(max-width: 831px) 100vw, 831px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Having been historically embedded in the higher education sector in the UK, the CloudPaging packaging technologies are now being recognised and breaking out into other industries and sectors. One of the main reasons – the claim that any application can be packaged is pretty much true. This is due to the unique way the technology can isolate or virtualize some part of an application and physically install others. The perennial problem of delivering device drivers as part of a virtual package is not a problem for CloudPaging. This is a major difference not to be overlooked when evaluating packaging tools.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><br>In tandem with the <a href="https://www.numecent.com/cloudpager/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">CloudPager</a>, which is Numecent’s application container management platform, you can easily and quickly deploy any application to a Windows desktop without installing it. The application can be a Cloudpaging app, AppV or MSIX and can be instantly updated or rolled back with no downtime or restarts.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="986" height="745" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Numecent-Apps.png" alt="Numecent CloudPager Applications" class="wp-image-7253" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Numecent-Apps.png 986w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Numecent-Apps-300x227.png 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Numecent-Apps-768x580.png 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 986px) 100vw, 986px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is particularly useful if you manage Virtual Desktops such as <a href="https://www.citrix.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Citrix</a>, <a href="https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/products/virtual-desktop">AVD</a> or <a href="https://www.parallels.com/products/ras/remote-application-server/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Parallels</a> – no need to have any applications in your base template or “gold image”.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="458" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Numecent-Platform-1024x458.png" alt="Numecent CloudPaging Platform" class="wp-image-7252" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Numecent-Platform-1024x458.png 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Numecent-Platform-300x134.png 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Numecent-Platform-768x343.png 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/Numecent-Platform.png 1112w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Some benefits of Numecent’s CloudPaging and CloudPager technologies include:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Accelerated deployment and management</li>



<li>Simplified base templates and dynamic application delivery for VDI</li>



<li>Improved compatibility and legacy software support</li>



<li>Enhanced security and compliance</li>



<li>Simplified application updates and patch management</li>



<li>Optimised performance and end-user experience</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Numecent’s innovative approach to application packaging through Cloudpaging revolutionizes software deployment by making it faster, more cost-effective, and more secure. Whether your organization is dealing with complex software rollouts, legacy application support, or the need for greater flexibility, Numecent CloudPaging provides a powerful solution that enhances efficiency while reducing IT overhead.</p>
					</div>

				</article>
								<article id="post-6481" class="post-6481 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-general category-memcm category-microsoft category-sccm">
					<header>
						<h1>The end of the road for Microsoft Deployment Toolkit (MDT)!</h1>					</header>

					<div>
						
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>The end of the road for Microsoft Deployment Toolkit</em> (<em>MDT)!</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/configmgr/mdt/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Microsoft Deployment Toolkit (MDT)</a> is a free Microsoft solution designed to simplify and automate the deployment of Windows Operating Systems and applications.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It has been the “go-to” tool set for IT professionals for decades and provides tools to create, customize, automate and manage Windows images across multiple devices.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">However, from October 10 2025, Microsoft is deprecating the Microsoft Deployment Toolkit (MDT) integration with Configuration Manager (ConfigMgr/SCCM). Continuing to use it beyond this date may cause corruption with Task Sequences, and will not be supported.&nbsp;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="869" height="176" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/MDT.png" alt="Microsoft Deployment Toolkit" class="wp-image-6482" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/MDT.png 869w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/MDT-300x61.png 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/MDT-768x156.png 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 869px) 100vw, 869px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Continuing to use it beyond this date may cause corruption with Task Sequences, and will not be supported. </p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading">Do you utilise MDT either as standalone infrastructure, or integrated into ConfigMgr?</h4>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">To make sure you migrate easily without issues, organizations should review their use of MDT and plan to move its features to other solutions.</p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading">How Workspace Can Help:</h4>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Here at <a href="https://workspace-it.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Workspace IT</a> our extensive product knowledge around ConfigMgr and MDT can help you understand the size of the problem:</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">One of our consultants will complete a remote assessment to understand and document your organisations reliance on MDT, the integration with ConfigMgr, legacy scripts in use, and deprecated functionality that may require alternative solutions.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Workspace IT will provide you with a migration plan, detailing recommendations to complete a smooth transition away from MDT, minimising disruption to production systems.</p>



<h4 class="wp-block-heading">Get Started Today - Prepare for MDT deprecation.</h4>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Contact us to schedule your assessment and receive a tailored migration strategy.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ref: <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/intune/configmgr/core/plan-design/changes/deprecated/removed-and-deprecated-cmfeatures" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Deprecated features - Configuration Manager | Microsoft Learn</a></p>
					</div>

				</article>
								<article id="post-5684" class="post-5684 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-charity category-general category-sun-screen-it">
					<header>
						<h1>Ghana 2025 - My Journal.</h1>					</header>

					<div>
						
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Written by Dan Goss - My Journal. </em></p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">The Sun Screen IT Mission</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>To end E-Waste and the illegal dumping of millions of tonnes of toxic computer waste every year. </li>



<li>To provide IT access in the form of sustainable, energy efficient Thin Client labs to developing countries.</li>



<li>Changing lives with volunteers sharing IT and teaching skills enhancing the learning environment for underprivileged children globally. </li>
</ul>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">My Journal</h3>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Medaase - Thank you</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">“Medaase” to all the people who supported me in joining <a href="https://www.sunscreenitfoundation.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Sun Screen IT Foundation</a> on their latest mission to deliver IT labs to 2 schools in Akropong, Ghana. The experience was unbelievable, and I am incredibly grateful to have had the opportunity to make a real difference and meet many unforgettable people along the way.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The local language in the village of Akropong is "Twi". Thank you in Twi is Medaase.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">To keep the memories fresh and to give my personal view and experiences throughout the journey I write this post. I hope to convey the gratitude and emotions I experienced while in Ghana.</p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Saturday 1<sup>st</sup> February 2025 – The dream team assembled. </h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Myself. Volunteer - Laurence Tucker, Operations Director extraordinaire. Charity Trustee and tech wizard - Steven Jones. Charity Founder - Nathaniel Comer, the change the world needs.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Now I was fortunate enough to see the enthusiasm and thankfulness of the people we would be visiting before we arrived which settled any anxiety I was feeling. This was due to a message received from the Headmistress of one of the schools we would be visiting.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>“Good evening. We wanted to express our heartfelt gratitude for your unwavering love and support towards our students. The Akropong Community is truly proud of your contributions. We eagerly look forward to welcoming you soon! God richly bless you.”</em></p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Sunday 2<sup>nd</sup> February 2025 – Let’s go!</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Now if like me you thought transporting equipment via airplane would be a doddle, you couldn’t be more wrong :-D. We started early, packing 10 suitcases!! We needed to wrap equipment securely to ensure they arrived in one piece after each bag made its way through the airport to the plane and back to us in Ghana. This was no simple task, imagine trying to transport 3 suitcases weighing around 30kgs each along with hand luggage, laptops etc.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="598" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_1-1024x598.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5687" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_1-1024x598.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_1-300x175.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_1-768x449.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_1-1536x897.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_1.jpg 1808w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thankfully after a smooth yet full flight with British Airways, we arrived on time in Accra and retrieved 10 still in one-piece suitcases… phew! Challenge 1 completed.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Upon arrival in Ghana I was unsure what to expect but the airport was smooth, well developed and we managed to get through passport control without issue. The first sign I noticed was a single huge word “Akwaaba” – Welcome.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After finding our transport, driver Albert and our dedicated helper Ben we set off on the hour-long journey to the village of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Akropong" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Akropong</a>. We made it to our hotel around 11:30pm. A long but well executed day.</p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Monday 3<sup>rd</sup> February – This is Africa!</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">First up, an early breakfast of Bread, Sausage, Egg and Salad with a topping of Beans (Like Heinz), different but pleasantly surprised.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Next, we set off on our 10–15-minute journey to check out the first of the 2 schools to make sure it was in the state we would expect and decide if we needed to make some adjustments or new plans.</p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_2-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5689" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_2-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_2-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_2-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_2-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_2.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_3-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5690" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_3-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_3-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_3-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_3-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_3.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div></div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">On arrival at the Presbyterian Kindergarten &amp; Primary School (PPS), my eyes were wide open with wonder and excitement. On exiting the van, I quickly realised my excitement was pale in comparison to the absolute beacons of smiling, happy faces of the students once they saw we were there.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1003" height="566" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_41.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5812" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_41.png 1003w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_41-300x169.png 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_41-768x433.png 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1003px) 100vw, 1003px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The IT room, that had been prepared for our arrival was in great condition, we had working electrics and network cables. Desks, chairs and benches for the students. Amazing! In this picture aside from the dream team from left to right we can see the Headmistress, Joseph (Electrician), Daniel Okeyre (Teacher) and Ben (Our local helper).</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_4-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5692" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_4-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_4-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_4-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_4-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_4.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After a quick check of the building everything looked good so we hopped back in the van and headed off to the second school we would be providing IT to. The PCE Demonstration Primary and Asamoah K.G School. The school is part of a campus, it has multiple schools within including the JHS school which Sun Screen IT Foundation delivered an IT lab to back in April 2025.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="595" height="349" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_5.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5693" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_5.png 595w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_5-300x176.png 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 595px) 100vw, 595px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Again, another ready to go room, freshly painted, some left-over monitors in place from the previous deployment at JHS. Cabling all neatly hidden in some trunking. At this point, the 4 of us were very happy to see 2 well-prepared rooms. Quite the opposite to some previous deployments I learnt from some of the war stories we talked about during our time together.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Now back to the smiling, happy faces I mentioned… I have no words to adequately convey the pure joy these children expressed each and every single time they saw us. I really have never been so popular. The chants and call outs of “Obroni” (white man) will stay with me forever.</p>



<div style="width: 50%; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/EZBkWweWZ2c" title="Ghana 1 - VID 20250203 WA0010" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;"></iframe>
    </div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After a few minutes in the room the children could not contain themselves and were flooding into the room to ask what was happening, what we were doing so the head teacher, Christian Anane, called an assembly to introduce us to the 100s of eager children and explain why we were there and what we would be doing.</p>



<div style="width: 50%; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/fwbQOJ-hA1M" title="Ghana 2 - VID 20250203 WA0009" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;"></iframe>
    </div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After some inspirational words from Nathaniel to the children, we stopped quickly at the JHS school to see how they are getting on with their delivery back in April and everyone was very happy to see a bustling busy classroom.</p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_6-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5694" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_6-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_6-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_6-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_6-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_6.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_7-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5695" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_7-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_7-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_7-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_7-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_7.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div></div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We headed back to the hotel to regroup and start preparing the IT kit into 2 lots to configure and transport to each school. Now you might think this was all glamour and comfortable, in reality we had 2 techies crouched on a bed configuring and testing 60 Thin clients, 2 Servers and 2 Switches. The other 2 were working through the cases organising and separating ready for transport when ready. All in a small, very hot, very humid hotel room.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Disaster</strong> – One of the switches appeared to have broken during transport and the monitors we sourced in Ghana had different display outputs to what the thin clients had. Ben our helper sprang into action speaking to contacts all around Accra to try to source the needed equipment and replacements.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Late evening, we experienced our first “doom so” or “off on” – a power cut that knocked out power everywhere without a generator for around 1hr. Nothing we could do now except sit on some plastic chairs and enjoy a cold refreshing bottle of Star beer. </p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Tuesday 4<sup>th</sup> February – Visit to Accra &amp; PCE Demo</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">8am start, today we split into 2 teams, Steven and I headed into one of the schools to get started while the others headed into Accra to find and purchase the bits we needed. A couple of hours they needed…. At 7.30pm, they arrived back at the hotel with everything we needed. This is commonly referred to as “African time”.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Meanwhile Steven and I had a successful day getting most of the devices on desks and had them connecting to the servers. It was starting to come together nicely.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_8-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5697" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_8-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_8-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_8-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_8-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_8.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Around midday, I had the absolute pleasure to meet Michaella and Christabel who came into the room and asked me “How do you type?”</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Now I will admit, for someone in a computer tech role for many years, I found it quite challenging to reset my mind to realise these students had never had a keyboard in front of them, or a mouse and really didn’t know how to use them.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Christabel – Left, Michaella – Right.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_9-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5698" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_9-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_9-300x225.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_9-768x576.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_9-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_9.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">These two 8 year old girls were beautiful, happy souls and spent a good half an hour talking with me, I learnt their favourite book is “The Red Hunter”, they love their teachers and coming to school. They have many friends, girls not the boys of course.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I showed them how to type while I was using my laptop and then with a computer keyboard. They knew all the letters and they took the keyboard and spent 20 minutes practising on the keyboard that at this point was not connected to a computer. Once they finished, they were asking me how to change the desktop background – an interesting question from someone who had never used a computer, but I spent some time showing them how on my laptop, they then both had a go and were extremely excited and happy to get to do it. They then hurried back to class.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At the end of school, they both re-appeared, Michaella had to stay at school to wait for her older sister and Christabel had to wait daily 2-3 hours for her driver to arrive and take her home. Can you imagine, 2-3hrs of waiting at school every day?</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The girls brought me a book to take back and read… to be continued</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="722" height="1024" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_10-722x1024.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5699" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_10-722x1024.jpg 722w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_10-212x300.jpg 212w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_10-768x1089.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_10-1083x1536.jpg 1083w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_10.jpg 1128w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 722px) 100vw, 722px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Around 5pm the school was closed, all lessons finished but some of the older students came to pray. Now I am talking about 100s of students, ages ranging from 6 to 23, all what to me sounded like cheering/chanting/singing. You could feel and I really mean you could feel the passion and might during this time. I recorded the sound to replay, at this point I was not sure if it might be disrespectful to video so decided not to.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-audio aligncenter"><audio controls src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Ghana-Audio-1.mp3"></audio></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At the end of the day, Mr Anane gave us a lift home in his car, it drove but for much longer I am not sure. Every light that could be lit on the dashboard, was lit.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_11-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5701" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_11-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_11-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_11-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_11-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_11.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Upon returning to the Hotel, we were shown some footage of the trip to Accra, I have some images from what was seen by Laurence and Nathaniel in the multiple IT shops, quite unbelievable.</p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="816" height="459" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_11.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5702" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_11.png 816w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_11-300x169.png 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_11-768x432.png 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 816px) 100vw, 816px" /></figure>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="823" height="456" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_12.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5703" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_12.png 823w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_12-300x166.png 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_12-768x426.png 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 823px) 100vw, 823px" /></figure>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="767" height="551" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_13.png" alt="" class="wp-image-5704" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_13.png 767w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Journal_13-300x216.png 300w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 767px) 100vw, 767px" /></figure>
</div></div>
</div>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Wednesday 5<sup>th</sup> February – All hands to the pump!</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">An earlier start today, meet for breakfast at 7am, not feeling particularly refreshed after a 20-minute dribbling shower but nevertheless we were up and raring to go again.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Today was about major progress so we split into 3 teams, Nathaniel headed down to the JHS schools to do some interviews with the students who had been using the computers since April.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Steven and I went back to PCE Demo to finish up some bits and pieces now we had the other monitors, cables and replacement parts. Laurence headed to the PPS school to get started setting up the computers, monitors and cabling at that school.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With DJ Nathaniel upfront in the van we of course had some tunes to get us fired up for the day…</p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow">
