<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong><em>We must do something to stop this practice of “dumping” in areas of poverty and economic need.</em></strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Steven and I headed back to PCE Demo school for some final configuration changes and enhancements. A morning not without some adventure, we thought we got lucky with a Mercedes that came to pick us up, a local guy Mr Darko borrowed it while we ate breakfast for 10 minutes and returned 30 minutes later with this taxi as the Merc had broken down. Now remember we are transporting equipment, in a case for protection…</p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="2000" height="1500" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_22.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5718" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_22.jpg 2000w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_22-300x225.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_22-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_22-768x576.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_22-1536x1152.jpg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2000px) 100vw, 2000px" /></figure>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="2000" height="1126" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_23.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5719" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_23.jpg 2000w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_23-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_23-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_23-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_23-1536x865.jpg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2000px) 100vw, 2000px" /></figure>
</div></div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We managed the 10-minute drive with the boot open, squashed in this tiny taxi without any further hiccups 😀</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Today we had the pleasure of being visited by a force of nature, Hilda, 22, a student teacher in her 4<sup>th</sup> year with 1 year left to go before she qualifies and gets her own teaching role. Hilda stood out from the crowd due to her enthusiasm, happiness and general demeanour, we talked for a couple of hours about all things Ghana and the United Kingdom. Hilda was floating around the room, gently singing to herself while swaying side to side whenever not being engaged in conversation, this was a common theme with Ghanian people in general and it was amazing to see.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This is Hilda, aka TikTok phenom and aspiring Journalist. She has 9,500 TikTok followers @miss_fenteng</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hilda told me she uses TikTok to release educational content and practise her journalism by interviewing others. She has also been interviewed and appeared on TV in Ghana. I have no doubt she has an incredibly bright future whatever she decides to do. The brief TikToks she had me watched looked very professional, nothing like the TikTok videos I have seen floating around the internet back at home.</p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1126" height="2000" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_24.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5721" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_24.jpg 1126w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_24-169x300.jpg 169w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_24-577x1024.jpg 577w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_24-768x1364.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_24-865x1536.jpg 865w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1126px) 100vw, 1126px" /></figure>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1275" height="1700" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_25.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5722" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_25.jpg 1275w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_25-225x300.jpg 225w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_25-768x1024.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_25-1152x1536.jpg 1152w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1275px) 100vw, 1275px" /></figure>
</div></div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hilda, as an educator took great pleasure in helping correctly spell some of Twi words, I had been making notes of to try and learn some of the local language. For reference, those notes are as follows:</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Medaase - Thank you</li>



<li>On off - Doom so</li>



<li>Kofi - Friday</li>



<li>Bra Yaw - Brother Thursday</li>



<li>Akwaaba - Welcome</li>



<li>Nyame nhyira wo - God bless you</li>



<li>Mimowachi - Good morning</li>



<li>Maajo - Good evening</li>



<li>Ete sen - How are you</li>



<li>Obroni - White person</li>



<li>Aye yeah - Good/Cool</li>



<li>Papa - Good</li>



<li>Yanko - Let's go</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Bra, is a respectful term, Yaw is the word for Thursday, Bra Yaw is how I would be called instead of Daniel, people are often called using the day they were born. Example, Laurence was known as Kofi Laurence during his time in Ghana.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We regrouped at the hotel around 6pm to prepare for a dinner with lots of the people we were working with in the area. Nathaniel, arranged for around 20 people to have dinner at a local restaurant with the help of Joseph, our main local contact. In another example of “<strong>African Time</strong>”, this was scheduled for a 7pm start, approximately 9pm we arrived while others were still arriving…</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">What an evening, music, beautiful people, new friends, started and finished with a prayer from the local pastor We got to meet some of the peoples families, wives and children. A special evening that ended in some African dancing which we all “tried” to take part in, some more successfully than others (A+ to Laurence!). A core memory locked in.</p>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="2000" height="1500" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_26.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5726" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_26.jpg 2000w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_26-300x225.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_26-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_26-768x576.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_26-1536x1152.jpg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2000px) 100vw, 2000px" /></figure>
</div></div>



