<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Friday 7<sup>th</sup> February – Mission Complete!!</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">My favourite day, an incredibly long, emotional roller coaster where all the work came to a head, and we were rewarded with a truly magical day.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">First up, we headed down to the PPS school to see Daniel and Joseph deliver their first lesson to the children. On arrival at the school, we received a warm welcome by some of the students clapping as we walked towards the classroom for the final time.</p>



<div style="width: 50%; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/jpYD2dz706Q" title="Ghana 7 - VID 20250207 WA0015" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;"></iframe>
    </div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The dream team excited and ready to see the students enter for their first lesson.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_27-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5732" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_27-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_27-300x225.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_27-768x576.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_27-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_27.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Here we go, Daniel &amp; Joseph delivering the first lesson on Microsoft PowerPoint, how to open it, select a template, type your name and add an animation – MAGIC!</p>



<div style="width: 50%; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/LaI03-kOigU" title="Ghana 8 - 20250207 092731" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;"></iframe>
    </div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Something I wanted to do was donate some pens and pencils to the school along with some sweets from the UK for the students to try. At the end of the lesson, Daniel handed each student a Moam ball shaped sweet as a well done to them. A huge success, once the flavours hit the faces lit up and it was beautiful to watch after a wonderful lesson given by the two teachers. </p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_28-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5735" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_28-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_28-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_28-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_28-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_28.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<div style="width: 50%; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/-Aqg-lNahnc" title="Ghana 9 - 20250207 093222" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;"></iframe>
    </div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As a final step, a message was left on the whiteboard which was also signed by the 4 of us.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>DREAM BIG WORK HARD</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After some goodbyes, one of who was Felicia who I mentioned earlier, we headed to the PCE Demo school.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Teacher “Sir Confidence” gave a lesson in this fully kitted out room, the floor changed overnight, curtains and posters to finish it off. The lesson consisted of how to use the mouse and keyboard, how to create and rename a folder and change the desktop background.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_29-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5738" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_29-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_29-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_29-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_29-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_29.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After the lesson finished up, we were in for something extraordinary, a ceremony of sorts that I cannot express in words but hope the following pictures and videos can at least show what we experienced.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We are asked to sit front and centre, on some black leather chairs, in 38c heat, without really knowing what to expect. Slowly we were joined by head teachers, village chiefs, a pastor and so on. The ceremony lasted around 2hrs, an incredible amount of thanks and appreciation was given to us, along with being given some traditional clothing each. This was without a doubt my trip highlight and I feel incredibly lucky to have been able to take part and witness it. I am not afraid to admit, I was filled with emotion throughout and had to wipe my eyes a few times (It must of been the dust).</p>



