<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1126" height="2000" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_32.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5746" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_32.jpg 1126w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_32-169x300.jpg 169w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_32-577x1024.jpg 577w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_32-768x1364.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_32-865x1536.jpg 865w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1126px) 100vw, 1126px" /></figure>
</div></div>



<div class="wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow"><div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1126" height="1690" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_33.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5747" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_33.jpg 1126w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_33-200x300.jpg 200w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_33-682x1024.jpg 682w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_33-768x1153.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_33-1023x1536.jpg 1023w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1126px) 100vw, 1126px" /></figure>
</div></div>
</div>



<div style="width: 50%; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/4tShWGSzHEM" title="Ghana 14 - VID 20250208 WA0005" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;"></iframe>
    </div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Money being given to the dancers was a sign of respect that they had done a great job. We thought they all did a great job, and we were later told that its tradition the money is shared amongst the dancers.<br><br>Upon questioning Albert (our driver) later, he explained that the dancing all had meaning, the colours of the clothing, the patterns on the clothing, the arm movements, everything meant something. Some examples he explained:<br><br>Colours often relate to the tribes, the black outfit symbolises a hunter. It then made sense as one of the movements looked like a throat being cut, we were told that this is protection for us against all enemies behind us.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Other movements included an expression of unity, coming together. The pointing up referenced god above all. As the ceremony concluded, the IT lab was officially opened.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_34-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5756" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_34-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_34-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_34-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_34-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_34.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Now we had to nip back to the PPS school as we forgot something and saw the only “bit” of rain throughout our visit. The sky went dark, real fast.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_35-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5758" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_35-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_35-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_35-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_35-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_35.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Luckily, we had made it inside the school as the rain arrived in force!</p>



<div style="width: 50%; margin: 0 auto;">
    <div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/vvyxUySVeuk" title="Ghana 16 - 20250207 183445" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;"></iframe>
    </div>
</div>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As quick as it came, it stopped after around 15 minutes, we headed back to the hotel to get the rest of our stuff before leaving for our return flight. We said our final goodbyes and headed home.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As I have mentioned them throughout, I would like to introduce Ben (front and center), 29, our helper, aspiring Chef. Ben was our 5<sup>th</sup> team member while out in Ghana and made things easier when we would have been struggling otherwise. He stayed with us for the week but he kindly invited us to his house to introduce his wife Esther, son Wind, and their 2 dogs, “Next time” and “Roly”.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="811" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_36-1024x811.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5760" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_36-1024x811.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_36-300x237.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_36-768x608.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_36-1536x1216.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_36.jpg 2048w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Also pictured from left to right. Nathaniel, Laurence, Steven and me – The Dream Team.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And finally, Albert, our driver, the man who got us where we needed to be and never left our side. Albert drives for a living but is also a mechanic, has a wife and 2 boys who took great pleasure seeing the Obroni via video call. Albert was a fount of knowledge; he managed to answer my many questions throughout our time together and give insight into the Ghanian way of life which was greatly appreciated.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="768" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_37-1024x768.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5762" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_37-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_37-300x225.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_37-768x576.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_37-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_37.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Upon arrival home, I was greeted with this picture hung in the window. After 7 days away from my family, seeing two smiling faces eagerly waiting for me as I opened the front door was an amazing feeling.</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="577" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_38-1024x577.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-5763" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_38-1024x577.jpg 1024w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_38-300x169.jpg 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_38-768x432.jpg 768w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_38-1536x865.jpg 1536w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/02/Journal_38.jpg 2000w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>
</div>


<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Ghana 2025 key takeaways</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The Ghanian way of life is so full of love, energy and respect it was a real joy to see. Many of them don't have much in comparison to people in the UK but you really wouldn't know it by their attitudes, everyone was super friendly, wanted to help and showed a huge amount of enthusiasm. I have no concerns that the two IT labs won't be used, the teachers and students could not wait to get in and start using them. Before i finished writing this I received a view from Daniel at the PPS school showing another lesson in progress with him explaining everyone is loving the IT lab and the students gave a big shout out to Sun Screen IT - AMAZING.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">A couple of quotes heard throughout the week will stay with me:</span><br><strong>"I have never seen so many people, working so hard, so slowly"<br>"DREAM BIG WORK HARD"<br>"I might be able to make a difference, so therefore I must" <br>"You can be the change"</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">And finally, for the techies among us that might be interested I made a note of what was deployed at each school.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Hardware:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>1x APC BX UPS</li>



<li>1x TPLink Omada Access Point</li>



<li>1x Cisco 2960 48 Port Switch</li>



<li>1x Physical Server running Proxmox Hypervisor</li>



<li>7x Virtual Servers, including Infrastructure services and an RDS Farm</li>



<li>30x IGEL UD3 Thin Client devices</li>



<li>8x Lenovo ThinkPad Laptops</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Software:</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Infrastructure Services
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Domain Controller</li>



<li>IGEL UMS</li>



<li>File Server</li>
</ul>
</li>



<li>RDS Farm
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Office 365 Apps </li>



<li>ScratchJr</li>



<li>Rapid Typing</li>



<li>Kiwix</li>



<li>Scratch </li>



<li>Inkspace</li>



<li>Gimp </li>



<li>Visual Studio Code</li>



<li>HTML Games including Space Invaders! (I noticed a young boy wearing a Space Invaders jumper on our first day to had to get this for them).</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
					</div>

				</article>
								<article id="post-4312" class="post-4312 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-general category-hardware category-igel category-lenovo category-sustainability">
					<header>
						<h1>Carbon Positive DaaS - Environmentally Friendly Devices</h1>					</header>

					<div>
						
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Carbon Positive DaaS - Environmentally Friendly Devices</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At Workspace IT, we’re setting a new standard in device management with our <strong>affordable, sustainable managed solutions</strong>. We believe we are the UK’s first Managed Service Provider to offer a carbon-positive - fully managed service, we are committed to helping you manage your IT devices in a way that reduces costs while prioritizing environmental responsibility and ethical practices. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Whether you’re optimizing existing devices or upgrading to new ones, our services align with your values and business needs.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Energy Efficient Endpoints.</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The new devices we deploy, such as those from <a href="https://www.lenovo.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener"><strong>Lenovo</strong></a>, are selected for their low energy consumption and compliance with leading environmental standards, including <strong>Energy Star</strong>, <strong>EPEAT</strong>, <strong>RoHS</strong>, and <strong>TCO Certified 9.0</strong>. These devices also meet <strong>Volatile Organic Compound (VOC)</strong> certification &amp; <strong>ERP Lot 3 and Lot 7 requirements</strong>, ensuring they contribute to a greener IT environment.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="991" height="380" src="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/CPDaaS-7.png" alt="CPDaaS-7" class="wp-image-4510" srcset="https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/CPDaaS-7.png 991w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/CPDaaS-7-300x115.png 300w, https://workspace-it.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/CPDaaS-7-768x294.png 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 991px) 100vw, 991px" /></figure>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">50-60% Reduction in energy cost</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Additional savings due to lower cost devices.</p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Scope 3 Emissions</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Product Carbon Footprint (PCF) documents for Scope 3 reporting CO2 Offset included with every device deployed.</p>



<hr class="wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-default" style="margin-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10)"/>



<div class="wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex">
